WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.860
[SHOUTING]

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.700
Actually, it's Wednesday, but
I did get 1400 people to say

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.740
hello to you with VidCon,
which isn't nothing.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.250
So Hank, we're just back
from VidCon, and for your

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.290
edification, I have compiled
my top ten VidCon moments.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.150
Number ten is dancing to the
All Caps song, Don't Unplug Me.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.790
and I think as you know I can't
dance, but I am very

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:18.850
passionate about it.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.240
The same way I felt about
French kissing in high school.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:28.550
[MUSIC]

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:29.310
Number nine.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:33.400
Meekakitty's velociraptor.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.930
Scary, but also alluring.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.430
Eight, Dan Brown's
announcement of Dan 3.0.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.822
For one year, I am very
literally putting complete

00:00:41.822 --> 00:00:43.700
control of my life
in your hands.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.050
Hank, I think Dan 3.0 will be a
fascinating social experiment.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.990
Although I fear that if we did
it, people would just make us

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.540
put unicorns on our
head all the time.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.250
Number seven.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:53.670
Hi I'm Rawn asked me dress up
as a turkey for his big musical

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:55.910
production. and I was pulling
on the turkey costume, and I

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.200
was like, Ron, that's fine,
I'm happy to do it,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:58.840
but I don't know.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.460
Am I supposed to dance?

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.910
Am I supposed to get on stage?

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.180
Whereupon he turned to a guy
dressed as Batman, pointed at

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.030
him, and said Batman, I'm
going to need you to be a

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.300
leader in this situation.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:07.885
Number six.

00:01:07.885 --> 00:01:11.180
Hank, singing on stage with
you for the first and

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:12.620
last time in my life.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.430
Put stuff on your head.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.610
Put stuff on your head.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:19.520
[UNINTELLIGIBLE]

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:20.885
to be red.

00:01:20.885 --> 00:01:25.935
The color doesn't matter
if it's on your head.

00:01:25.935 --> 00:01:29.320
[APPLAUSE]

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.070
Number five.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:32.640
Mass hug at the Nerdfighter
gathering involving

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.170
hundreds of Nerdfighters.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:34.580
Four.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.730
I suppose at this point I
should be used to it, but Ze

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.810
Frank gave the most
astonishingly brilliant keynote

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.410
address I think I have ever
heard, reminding us that we

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.980
don't make or watch videos for
money or subscribers or

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.670
reviews, but because we want to
feel what it's like to be other

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.500
people and let others feel what
it's like to be us.

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:51.220
Number three.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:52.590
Just how nice everyone was.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.610
I mean, given the fact that
YouTubers are mostly

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.350
introverted, nerdy people who
like to spend their free time

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.440
with editing software.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.970
Everyone was incredibly nice.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:01.960
Everyone hung out.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.020
Famous people didn't act
like they were famous.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.080
And the whole vibe of the event
was so wonderfully supportive

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.190
and collaborative.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.280
Number two.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.390
Two words.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.850
Double Rainbow.

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.910
The Gregory Brothers of
Auto-Tune the News singing

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:17.560
a song they had written
mere hours before.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:22.420
This is a song that goes
out to all the rainbows.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:31.020
Also the ladies.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.450
But mostly the rainbows.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:40.300
Double rainbow all the way
across the sky, yeah yeah.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.602
It's so intense.

00:02:42.602 --> 00:02:49.838
[MUSIC AND CHEERING]

00:02:49.838 --> 00:02:51.270
And number one.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:54.650
Seeing my little brother sing
about particle physics in front

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:58.400
of a thousand people who
loved every second of it.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.364
A quark is a fundamental
constituent of matter,

00:03:00.364 --> 00:03:02.545
observed in 1968 through
deep elastic scatter.

00:03:02.545 --> 00:03:04.777
We found that protons aren't
as simple as we thought.

00:03:04.777 --> 00:03:07.300
We thought they were solid
particles, but they are not.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.310
Nerdfighters.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.860
Hank, thank you for all the
thousands of hours you

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.800
spent making VidCon
as awesome as it was.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:16.740
It felt like my favorite parts
of the internet existed in real

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.460
life for three whole days.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:21.590
Nerdfighters, if you were at
VidCon, whether in real life or

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.490
on live stream, please let us
know what your favorite parts

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:25.410
of the conference were.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.010
And let us know, if Hank is
crazy enough to do this whole

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:31.610
thing again, who and what you'd
like to see at VidCon 2011.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.550
So Hank, thanks again,
and I will see--

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.742
Hey listen, I'm happy for you,
and I don't know if you

00:03:35.742 --> 00:03:36.935
finished, but the Vlog Brothers
have one the most subscribed

00:03:36.935 --> 00:03:39.310
YouTube channels of all time.

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.910
That's right, the Vlog Brothers
just broke into the top

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:41.820
100 most subcribed.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.230
Thank you all for subscribing.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.240
Particularly thanks to
Ray William Johnson,

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.560
Charlieissocoollike,
and Meekakitty, but

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.350
thanks to everybody.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.200
You're so awesome.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.080
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

